# Force LF line endings for shell scripts regardless of the committer's or
# checkout machine's OS/git config. Without this, a Windows checkout can
# convert a script's line endings to CRLF, which corrupts its #!/bin/sh
# shebang line and breaks exec inside a Linux Docker image with a confusing
# "No such file or directory" error even though the file plainly exists.
# Found via metrics-agent/entrypoint.sh, 2026-09-05 (see that Dockerfile's
# own defense-in-depth `sed` normalization for the same root cause).
*.sh text eol=lf
